The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is

$$
\dfrac{\textrm{d}}{\textrm{d}x}(\arsech x) = -\dfrac{1}{x\sqrt{1-x^2}}.
$$

Using the formula above with the chain rule, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}\frac{\text{d}y}{\text{d}x} & =\frac{\text{d}}{\text{d}x}(5\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\  & =5\frac{\text{d}}{\text{d}x}(\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\  & =5(-\frac{1}{(2x)\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}})\cdot (2x)^{′} \\  & =-\frac{5}{2x\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\cdot 2 \\  & =-\frac{5}{x\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\end{aligned}
$$

